          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.109,
            0.744,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": "Deepa looked around her in the bus and noticed that all the passengers were seated. She looked around again after a minute and found them still occupying their seats. She wondered, ‘Are they moving?’ She concluded that the position of the passengers was not changing with time. Therefore, they were certainly at rest. However, when she looked outside, she felt they were in motion as their positions were changing with respect to things outside."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.278,
            0.744,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "The reference point is important in deciding whether an object is at rest or in motion. If Deepa considered herself (or the bus) as the reference point, then the passengers were at rest. However, if she considered any object outside the bus (say a building) as the reference point, then the passengers (and the bus) were in motion. Mor More to"
        },
        {
